<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_remainingAmount">
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#CustomerPayment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_status -->

<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_status">
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#CustomerPayment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#CustomerPaymentItem -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#CustomerPaymentItem">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Customer Payment ABE"/>
<rdf:label>CustomerPaymentItem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>CustomerPaymentItem is the application of CustomerPayment. CustomerPaymentItem is applied to CustomerBill or AppliedCustomerBillingRate.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_appliedAmount -->

<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_appliedAmount">
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#CustomerPaymentItem"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Dunning ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Dunning ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Customer Bill Collection ABE"/>
<rdfs:comment>The Dunning ABE represents attempts to collect payment from a customer for overdue payments.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Dunning ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasDomain_for_Dunning ABE -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasDomain_for_Dunning ABE">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasDomain"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Dunning ABE"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Domain"/>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1# hasBE_for_Dunning ABE -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasBE_for_Dunning ABE">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasBE"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Dunning ABE"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningCase"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningCaseRule"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningNotification"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningRule"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningScenario"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningWriteOff"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#HardDunning"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#SoftDunning"/>
<rdfs:comment>hasBE_for_Dunning ABE</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>hasBE_for_Dunning ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningCase -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningCase">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Dunning ABE"/>
<rdf:label>DunningCase</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The DunningCase represents a type of cases open for a customer. Whenever a customer enters the dunning process, a dunning case is linked to his billing account debt and it contains all details pertaining to the debt, such as dunning case rules, interactions The status of a dunning case evolves according to internal or external events (payments made by the customer, payment schedule granted).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_ID -->

<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_ID">
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningCase"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_startingDate -->

<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_startingDate">
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningCase"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningCaseRule -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningCaseRule">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Dunning ABE"/>
<rdf:label>DunningCaseRule</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The DunningCaseRule represents an action performed by the company (or on its behalf) to recover a debt.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_ID -->

<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_ID">
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningCaseRule"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_outbreakDate -->

<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_outbreakDate">
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningCaseRule"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningNotification -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#DunningNotification">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Dunning ABE"/>
<rdf:label>DunningNotification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A DunningNotification is a communication or joint activity from the Telecommunication Operator to the customer to ask for a CustomerPayment or negotiate a PaymentPlan.

The relation resulting from a DunningCaseRule might be 

 either only from the telecommunication operator to the customer (Ex: send a SMS) 

 or in both ways (Ex: a CSR call the customer to negotiate a PaymentPlan).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

