<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Product Order ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Product Order ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#ABE"/>
<rdfs:comment>The Product Order ABE contains all entities required to specify a communication used to procure or update one or many Products in the context of a ProductOffering. This pattern is used to define: 

 CustomerProductOrder corresponding to Products ordered by a Customer to the Service Provider 

 and BusinessPartnerProductOrder corresponding to Products ordered by the Service Provider to a Business Partner 

Note: Some but not all enterprises consider an Order to be a type of an Agreement. From a SID model perspective, an Order can be formalized by an Agreement and the Agreements relationship between the Agreement and the ProductOrder. This philosophy has the advantage of clearly separating two different concepts: the order from the legal formalisms associated with the order. For example, several orders may refer to the same Agreement.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Product Order ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

