<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#ResourceSpecRunsSoftwareSpec -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#ResourceSpecRunsSoftwareSpec">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Software Specification ABE"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceSpecRunsSoftwareSpec</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The association class is used to show the status of a SoftwareSpecification that can run on any ResourceSpecification.  For example, the status may reflect that it can or can no longer be run.  The association was made so that any type of resource (within reason!) could run Software, such as a CompoundResource, LogicalDevice or PhysicalDevice.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

