<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#SignalingProtocol -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#SignalingProtocol">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Signaling Protocols ABE"/>
<rdf:label>SignalingProtocol</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an abstract base class for representing different types of signaling protocols that can be managed. Signaling protocols are used to convey information along a specific path. This class represents a convenient aggregation point for defining how signaling protocols are managed and used.

The SID model defines COPS and RSVP as examples of subclasses of this class.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

