<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#WANProtocol -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#WANProtocol">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#WAN Protocols ABE"/>
<rdf:label>WANProtocol</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>WAN Protocols operate at the lowest three levels of the OSI model (i.e., physical, data link, and network) and are used to define communications over different types of wide-area media.

The SID model defines ATM, FrameRelay, HDLC, ISDN, PPP, SLIP, SMDS, and X.25 as examples of subclasses of this class.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

