<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Bay -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Bay">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#HolderComposite ABE"/>
<rdf:label>Bay</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A Bay is a type of EquipmentHolder that is designed to hold various types of Equipment. It has a logical identifier, usually a component of port AIDs in TL1 based switches.

Note that the logical identifier of a Bay is typically associated with the Device (i.e., the NetworkElement). This means that the Bay IS explicitly a part of the logical model of a network.

A Bay is usually built as a pre-wired hardware assembly that contains a set of shelves and accompanying ancillary Equipment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

