<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Physical Component ABE"/>
<rdf:label>ASIC</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An ASIC is an Application Specific Integrated Circuit.

This class represents a special type of Chip that is used to upgrade the functionality of a networking device. Examples include upgrading the modem function of a device, increasing the processing capability of a Card or Device, and implementing some type of networking functionality, such as fast switching, directly in hardware (as opposed to emulating it in software).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

