<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Closed Loop ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Closed Loop ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#ABE"/>
<rdfs:comment>Closedloop is a "management framework" in which current outcomes are used to improve future outcomes in order to achieve specified goals. The management framework includes the feedforward workflow and a feedback workflow, where the feedforward is a control loop meant to continually optimize and improve 
There can be different management frameworks, referred to in this model as "closedloop models". Optimized versions of closedloop management frameworks may be derived for specific scenarios. Closedloop can be typified as fast or slow and can work hierarchically or as peers or both, based on implementation choices.
For more information please refer to IG1219.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Closed Loop ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

