<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Criterion -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Criterion">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Segmentation ABE"/>
<rdf:label>Criterion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The Criterion is the definition of information classifying an Entity from the model (represented by an instance of RootEntityType).
A Criterion classifies only one RootEntityType, i.e. it helps grouping instances of only one Entity of the Orange SID model.
Examples:
         the Criterion Age classifies a Party (instance Party of RootEntityType)
         the Criterion Installation city classifies an InstalledResource
A Criterion might be
         either existing information related to an Entity
              in this case we need to specify where the information can be found 
                 the Attribute carrying the Criterion information (RootEntityTypeCharSpec)
                 the Entity carrying the Criterions Attribute
                 and the Relationship between the Entity classified by the Criterion and the Entity where the Criterion can be found (RelationshipType)
         or information that has to be calculated
              in this case we need a rule that specifies when it has to be calculated and how to calculate the information (cf. CriterionCalculationRule)
              the calculated information might be recorded or not. 
                 If not, it is only used to evaluate the condition for the Criterion. 
                 If yes, we need to specify where it has to be recorded
                      the Attribute carrying the Criterion information
                      the Entity carrying the Criterion Attribute
                      and the Relationship between the Entity concerned by the Criterion and the Entity where the Criterion is recorded
Note: 
         Only attributes carried by an Entity directly related to the Entity concerned by the Criterion can be specified to record the Criterions value.
         As many relationships might exist between the Entity classified and the Entity carrying the Criterion attribute, we may need to specify which type of relationship is concerned (RelationshipType)</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_ID -->

<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_ID">
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Criterion"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_name -->

<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_name">
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Criterion"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#CriterionCondition -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#CriterionCondition">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Segmentation ABE"/>
<rdf:label>CriterionCondition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A CriterionCondition specifies a condition expressed using Criteria.
A CriterionCondition might be Atomic or Composite.
Each AtomicCriterionCondition specifies a condition on a Criterion such as If Age = 36.
Each CompositeCriterionCondition combines two or more AtomicCriterionConditions specifying if all the AtomicCriterionConditions must be True (AND) or if at least one of them must be True (OR).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#CompositeCriterionCondition -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#CompositeCriterionCondition">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Segmentation ABE"/>
<rdf:label>CompositeCriterionCondition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Each CompositeCriterionCondition combines two or more AtomicCriterionConditions specifying if all the AtomicCriterionConditions must be True (AND) or if at least one of them must be True (OR).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_compositionType -->

<owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#hasAttr_compositionType">
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#CompositeCriterionCondition"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
</owl:DatatypeProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#AtomicCriterionCondition -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#AtomicCriterionCondition">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Segmentation ABE"/>
<rdf:label>AtomicCriterionCondition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Each AtomicCriterionCondition specifies a condition on a Criterion such as If Age = 36.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Segment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Segment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Segmentation ABE"/>
<rdf:label>Segment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A Segment is the result of applying a SegmentSpecification when a triggeringEvent occurs.
The validity period is calculated according to the triggering event.
The Segment classifies RootEntitys instances for which the CriterionCondition is True when it is built.
The attribute respectsThreshold specifies if the Segment respects the lower and upper size defined by the SegmentSpecification.
A Segment might be composite. A CompositeSegment corresponds to the sum of the composed Segments.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

