<rdf:label>AtomicVision</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A type of Vision that does not have any subordinate Vision, that is, an Atomic Vision is a leaf-level Vision.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#AtomicProjectDeliverable -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#AtomicProjectDeliverable">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Project ABE"/>
<rdf:label>AtomicProjectDeliverable</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A type of ProjectDeliverable that does not have any subordinate ProjectDeliverables, that is, an Atomic ProjectDeliverable is a leaf-level ProjectDeliverable.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#ProjectScope -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#ProjectScope">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Project ABE"/>
<rdf:label>ProjectScope</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The ProjectScope defines the "functional area" impacted by a project that can be expressed by eTOM process elements, SID entities and/or TAM application which might be effected by the project. In a multi-project environment (or a program) the scopes of those projects might be structured in a (composite) hierarchy.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

