</owl:DatatypeProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#MACAddressValue -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#MACAddressValue">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Policy Value ABE"/>
<rdf:label>MACAddressValue</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This class is used to define a list of MAC addresses and MAC address range values as an unordered list of strings, each specifying a MAC address or a range of MAC addresses according to the canonical 802 MAC address format. Each string entry is either:
- a single MAC address, such as 0000:00A5:0000
- a range of MAC addresses specified by an address
and mask, such as 0000:00A5:0000,FFFF:FFFF:0000,
which defines a range of MAC addresses in which the 
first four octets are equal to 0000:00A5.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

