<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#PolicyBrokerRole -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#PolicyBrokerRole">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#BE"/>
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#PolicyApp Role ABE"/>
<rdf:label>PolicyBrokerRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a concrete base class that defines the concept of various types of roles used to describe PolicyBrokers and their use in the model.
A PolicyBrokerRole refines the generic concepts of a PolicyApplicationRole. Specifically, this base class is used to describe generic functionality inherent in a PolicyBroker. For example, this includes the ability to present and negotiate functionality that is traded between different PolicyServers in different PolicyDomains, as well as the ability to control the functions of a PolicyServer.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

