<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Capacity ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#Capacity ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/InformationModel_v1#ABE"/>
<rdfs:comment>A generalized ABE and specializations that provide capacity and capacity demand for products, services, and resources.
Capacity is the ability to provide some capability.  For example, one measure of network capacity is the ability of a network to provide a certain amount of bandwidth during the month of May.
Capacity and the Business Process Framework (eTOM)
A number of eTOM Level 3 process elements were used as the basis for some of the requirements satisfied by this model.  They include the L3 processes, Produce Product Portfolio Business Plans. Produce Service Business Plans, and Produce Resource Business Plans, with L1 Strategy processes. And, the L3 processes, Enable Service Configuration and Activation and Enable Resource Provisioning, within the L1 Operations Support and Readiness processes.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Capacity ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

